{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDENDADwXfpfmPyMfzdB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"MATERIAL OBJECTION\n\n## (1) Fidelity\n\n**(a) §9: applied faithfully.** The added line matches the change list on every point:\n- **Trigger:** \"부재·배타 값(‘없음’, ‘0’, ‘~곡뿐’ 등)\"\n- **Scope:** the cell's own track, or \"해당 트랙들\" for a line under the table.\n- **Comparison set:** \"입력 블록, 열람한 페이지, 검색 결과\", ③'s other cells, and ②·⑤.\n- **Outcome:** the absence value is replaced by the item or its location.\n- **Disclosure:** the range is stated in the column head or legend for cells, and in the sentence for lines under the table.\n\nIt sits right after the ③ column list. It adds no recount and no numerator rule.\n\n**(b) §6: applied, with one wording problem (see 3).** The trigger, the comparison and the two outcomes are all present and in the right place: after \"빠진 역할의 종류를 적는다\" and before \"선별은 역할 단위로만 한다\".\n\n## (2) Scope\n\nNothing beyond the declared change. No album, outlet, service or track-specific fact is named. Both example strings are generic. Part (b) is the declared orchestrator extension.\n\n## (3) New defects\n\n**Objection: attribution upgrade in (b).** The added clause says:\n\n> 거기에 있으면 그 역할을 옮기거나 위치를 적는다.\n\nThe sentence before it is about transcribing one named credit row, such as a booklet or distributor page. As written, a role found somewhere else (a search snippet, or a fetch of a different page) can be \"옮기\" into that row. The appendix would then show it as part of the authoritative row. That upgrades the role's attribution, inflates its status, and hides from the auditor which source actually lists the role. That last point is what D6 depends on.\n\nIn (a) this is less of a risk, because ③ already has an evidence column.\n\nReplacement text:\n\n> 빠진 역할을 ‘받지 못했다’고 적기 전에 이미 받은 자료와 대조하고, 거기에 있으면 그 역할을 원래 출처와 함께 따로 옮기거나 위치를 적는다. 다른 출처에서 찾은 역할을 옮기고 있는 행에 합치지 않는다.\n\nThis adds about 60 bytes. It asks for no new section or list and no counting. It only says where an existing item goes.\n\n**Checked, no objection:**\n- **Defect 6:** (a) replaces a '~곡뿐' value with an item or a pointer. It does not ask for a recount, so it stays clear of round 3's edit 3.\n- **Length:** the range disclosure is one mention per column or sentence. A contradicted \"없음\" becomes a pointer, which is no longer than before.\n- **Spurious conflicts / quota-filling:** \"해당 항목\" is tied to the track, so it doesn't invite padding cells.\n- **Headless feasibility:** comparing against what the run has already received needs no new tool calls.\n- **Cuts:** nothing is removed, and the checklist and role-string rules are untouched.\n\n**Non-blocking:** (a) says \"5의 규칙\" while the same sentence uses \"②·⑤\" for output sections. If P5 cites sections as \"§5\", use \"§5의 규칙대로\". Otherwise leave it.\n\nOut of scope: none."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8779,"cache_read_input_tokens":1807,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8779},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dc08fc6-466f-45f6-893d-0120c8546f6f","uuid":"49f46fac-eec8-4337-b526-53e049cab4d2","timestamp":"2026-10-20T09:12:50.117Z","request_id":"req_011CgDENCneznYWpKsmudWj3"}
